{
  "description": "Known-answer test cases for the bolted joint calculator. Inputs and published answers come from the worked examples in Shigley's Mechanical Engineering Design, 10th ed., Chapter 8 (method summarized in docs/bolted-joint-reference.md). Units: inches, Mpsi for stiffness (Mlbf/in), kip for force, kpsi for stress. The book rounds intermediate values, so compare with a relative tolerance.",
  "tolerance_relative": 0.01,
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "shigley_ex_8_5",
      "title": "Cap screw into cast-iron base, fluctuating load (main target case)",
      "book_ref": "Example 8-5, book p. 440-442 (PDF p. 463-465)",
      "inputs": {
        "joint_type": "cap_screw",
        "thread": { "d": 0.625, "tpi": 11, "series": "UNC" },
        "grade": "SAE 5",
        "washer": { "t": 0.0625, "material": "hardened steel", "E_Mpsi": 30 },
        "top_member": { "t": 0.625, "material": "steel", "E_Mpsi": 30 },
        "tapped_member": { "t": 0.625, "material": "cast iron", "E_Mpsi": 16 },
        "cone_half_angle_deg": 30,
        "washer_face_diameter": "1.5d",
        "threaded_full_length_in_grip": true,
        "preload_rule": "0.75 * proof load (reused fastener)",
        "load_per_bolt_kip": { "P_min": 0, "P_max": 5 },
        "strengths_kpsi": { "Sp": 85, "Sut": 120, "Se": 18.6 }
      },
      "expected": {
        "At_in2": 0.226,
        "h_in": 0.6875,
        "grip_l_in": 1.0,
        "frusta": [
          { "name": "upper (steel, from washer face)", "t_in": 0.5, "D_in": 0.9375, "E_Mpsi": 30, "k_Mlbf_in": 46.46 },
          { "name": "middle (steel, rest of top plate)", "t_in": 0.1875, "D_in": 1.298, "E_Mpsi": 30, "k_Mlbf_in": 197.43 },
          { "name": "lower (cast iron)", "t_in": 0.3125, "D_in": 0.9375, "E_Mpsi": 16, "k_Mlbf_in": 32.39 }
        ],
        "km_Mlbf_in": 17.40,
        "kb_Mlbf_in": 6.78,
        "C": 0.280,
        "Fi_kip": 14.4,
        "n_p_yield": 1.22,
        "n_L_load_factor": 3.44,
        "n_0_separation": 4.00,
        "sigma_i_kpsi": 63.72,
        "sigma_a_kpsi": 3.10,
        "sigma_m_kpsi": 66.82,
        "n_f_goodman": 2.44,
        "proof_line_Sa_kpsi": 10.64,
        "n_proof_line": 3.43,
        "n_f_gerber": 3.65
      },
      "notes": "Grip uses l = h + d/2 because t2 >= d. The middle frustum's 197.43 is the book's figure; computing it unrounded gives about 197.6, still within tolerance. n_L is 3.44 with the book's rounded Fi = 14.4 kip and 3.43 unrounded. Goodman (2.44) says fatigue governs, but Gerber (3.65) is above the proof-line factor (3.43). The book points out this conflict."
    },
    {
